9
underscores the crucial role of chemically optimized surfaces in fostering the growth of more undifferentiated hPSCs compared to substrates with feeder cells, underscoring the superiority of these engineered surfaces. Figure
9
illustrates the physical changes applied to the polystyrene substrates, encompassing both chemical and geometrical modifications, which were pivotal in enhancing their performance. To further advance the engineered surfaces, the study employed computational modeling, as depicted in Fig.
